    "ERR-BASE"
  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-dao-1-err-1/ado-connection-errors: Errors.Clear ran with Count already 0 (a successful Execute had emptied it), so the clear effect was untested. On a new ADODB.Connection (Provider Microsoft.ACE.OLEDB.12.0, Data Source through Properties, Mode adModeRead): Connection.Errors read; Open; Errors read; Execute 'SELEC ID FROM T' (provider failure) and, with NO call in between, the held Errors object's Count and a fresh read of Errors; Errors.Clear on the held object; its Count and a fresh read. Then Execute 'SELECT * FROM NoSuchTable' (a second provider failure), the same reads, Clear, the same reads. Then a successful Execute of 'SELECT ID, V FROM T' and the Count. Asks what Errors.Clear does to entries that are present, and whether reading Errors changes them. The fixture copy is opened read-only through ADO.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
